sentences.text:
It is the case of the petitioner that as per the National Highways Act, 1956, Section 3G(1) provides that "where any land is acquired under this Act, there shall be paid an amount which shall be determined by an order to the competent authority."
Sub-Section (5) of Section 3G of the said Act states - "If the amount determined by the competent authority under Sub-Section (1) or Sub-Section (2) is not acceptable to either of the parties, the amount shall, on an application by either of the parties, be determined by the arbitrator to be appointed by the Central Government."
Sub-Section (7) of Section 3G states - "The competent authority or the arbitrator while determining the amount under Sub-Section (1) or Sub-Section (5), as the case may be, shall take into Adarsh Kumar Ram vs Union Of India & Ors on 18 October, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/5111168/
1 consideration - (a) the market value of the land on the date of publication of the notification under Section 3A;
(b) the damage, if any, sustained by the person interested at the time of taking possession of the land, by reason of the severing of such land from other land;
(c) the damage, if any, sustained by the person interested at the time of taking possession of the land, by reason of the acquisition injuriously affecting his other immovable property in any manner,
or his earnings;
(d) if, in consequences of the acquisition of the land, the person interested is compelled to change his residence or place of business, the reasonable expenses, if any, incidental to such change.
It is submitted by the learned Advocate on behalf of the petitioner that after taking over the land by way of acquisition the competent authority on his own whims and caprice determined the value of the land and structure.

